      "title": "Note: MOSS-Image",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image\n\nSettings from the MOSS prompting study: 20 steps, CFG 5, euler / sgm_uniform, SLG (uncond skip, layer 22, 0-1), empty negative, 1344x768. Prompt: prose, one sentence per element, no quality prefix.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: native 22 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 18 s, Manual (0.5x to step 10) 14 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here use **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): run once, paste the report's values into Automatic.\n2. **Automatic** (active): already set to this prompt's harvested values. At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the useful setting for images.\n3. **Manual** (muted): swap in for Automatic.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a native\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MOSS-Image\n\nSettings from the MOSS prompting study: 20 steps, CFG 5, euler / sgm_uniform, SLG (uncond skip, layer 22, 0-1), empty negative, 1344x768. Prompt: prose, one sentence per element, no quality prefix.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: native 22 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 18 s, Manual (0.5x to step 10) 14 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here use **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): run once, paste the report's values into Automatic.\n2. **Automatic** (active): already set to this prompt's harvested values. At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the useful setting for images.\n3. **Manual** (muted): swap in for Automatic.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a native\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
